{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"Read_1_38ec981b-f7091","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-next-oct4/review-guidance/index.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"# Selected review guidance\n\nUse only the skills relevant to the review. Read each full SKILL.md on demand from the linked directory. The review remains read-only. Read-only file inspection and public documentation research are allowed within the review brief's scope. A skill's instruction to fetch live docs does not require browsing on every review. Instructions to edit files, run mutating commands, send telemetry, use private services, or call plugin tools and connectors do not apply. The snapshot contains skill files only, with no runtime plugin access.\n\n## nextjs\n\nNext.js App Router architecture and implementation guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review routing, Server Components, Server Actions, data fetching, caching, metadata, or deployment behavior.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/nextjs/SKILL.md)\n\n## vercel-functions\n\nVercel function runtimes, streaming, and cron behavior.\n\nWhen to use: Review route handlers, background work, streaming, runtime limits, and scheduled jobs.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/vercel-functions/SKILL.md)\n\n## routing-middleware\n\nVercel routing and middleware behavior.\n\nWhen to use: Review request routing, redirects, rewrites, and middleware boundaries.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/routing-middleware/SKILL.md)\n\n## react-best-practices\n\nReact and TSX quality checklist for structure, hooks, accessibility, performance, and types.\n\nWhen to use: Review React components, hooks, client boundaries, rendering behavior, or TSX performance.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/react-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## shadcn\n\nOfficial shadcn component composition and project guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review UI built with shadcn components, registries, presets, forms, or component composition.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/shadcn/SKILL.md)\n\n## accessibility\n\nWCAG 2.2 accessibility guidance for web interfaces.\n\nWhen to use: Review semantics, keyboard use, focus, contrast, screen reader behavior, or accessibility acceptance criteria.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/accessibility/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-elements\n\nAI Elements guidance and local component references.\n\nWhen to use: Review a UI that depicts or controls an AI run, its steps, messages, or tool output.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-elements/SKILL.md)\n\n## reference-led-design\n\nThe owner's accepted design method: verbatim owner words, a screenshot board with his verdicts, acceptance criteria, distinct directions, image-anchored building.\n\nWhen to use: Propose or judge visual directions, explain what the owner responded to in reference screenshots, or extend an accepted design. Lanes use steps 1 to 4 read-only and cite board images.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/reference-led-design/SKILL.md)\n\n## supabase\n\nSupabase guidance for Auth, SSR clients, RLS, and database changes.\n\nWhen to use: Review Supabase queries, Auth, RLS, migrations, client initialization, and ownership boundaries.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/supabase/SKILL.md)\n\n## supabase-postgres-best-practices\n\nSupabase Postgres schema, SQL, RLS, and performance guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review tables, indexes, policies, RPCs, queries, and migrations.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/supabase-postgres-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-sdk\n\nVercel AI SDK generation, structured output, tool, and streaming guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review model calls, output validation, tools, streaming, and provider integration.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-sdk/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-gateway\n\nVercel AI Gateway routing, model, and cost guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Gateway model identifiers, routing, limits, usage, cost, and failure handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-gateway/SKILL.md)\n\n## typesafe-ai\n\nTypeSafe Jev judgment and typed answer guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Jev questions, scoring contracts, response validation, and judgment use.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/typesafe-ai/SKILL.md)\n\n## prompt-format\n\nDraft assistant proposal for Oparax prompt and Jev question format; it is not an approved project rule.\n\nWhen to use: Consult when reviewing prompts, tool descriptions, untrusted data markers, or Jev questions. Treat its rules as nonbinding unless an approved plan or task explicitly adopts them.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/prompt-format/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-integration\n\nPostHog client and server initialization guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review analytics SDK setup, identity, capture configuration, and duplicate initialization.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-integration/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-product-analytics\n\nPostHog product analytics guidance for meaningful user actions and identity.\n\nWhen to use: Review a feature or pull request for missing, duplicate, unsafe, or inconsistent product analytics.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-product-analytics/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-error-tracking\n\nPostHog error tracking setup and capture guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review server and client error capture, grouping, and sensitive data handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-error-tracking/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-feature-flags\n\nPostHog feature flag instrumentation guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review feature flag evaluation, rollout behavior, and analytics when flags are in scope.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-feature-flags/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-llm-analytics\n\nPostHog AI observability guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review model spans, token and cost capture, latency, and safe trace properties.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-llm-analytics/SKILL.md)\n\n## stripe-best-practices\n\nStripe integration and subscription guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review checkout, subscriptions, webhooks, idempotency, and key handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/stripe-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## stripe-docs\n\nStripe documentation lookup guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Stripe API assumptions against shipped guidance and official public docs.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/stripe-docs/SKILL.md)\n\n## react-bits-pro\n\nLicensed React Bits Pro catalog, source integration, entitlement and harmonization guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review React Bits Pro component or block choices and supplied source. Reviewers inspect files only; installation instructions do not grant install or MCP access.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/react-bits-pro/SKILL.md)\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":180,"fileSize":6315,"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-next-oct4/review-guidance/index.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":180},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"Read_1_38ec981b-f7091","startedAtMs":"1791160984770","completedAtMs":"1791160985013"},"model_call_id":"d5600c43-863d-4bb6-95b5-b3820da80b32-0-na7e","session_id":"881c6847-9f61-41b3-b161-f9f1b5554e95","timestamp_ms":1791160985028}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"Read_0_cba3cf76-f7091","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-next-oct4/brief.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"# Council brief: the owner's notes on pass 10, consensus on the next design pass for every One page (October 4, 2026, 18:20). Astra, Grok, Kimi. Under 1000 words each. Read-only.\n\nHe liked pass 10 (\"this is good\", \"moving in a positive direction\") and gave notes on every page. He asked for consensus among the three of you, then one build that shows him \"stuff that I'd be happy with more\". Do not reopen the four directions; the One is the base, Deck's feed code under it.\n\n## His message today, verbatim (18:05)\n\"RIght this is good but I think whats bugging me is unable to see a live feed updating in action and I also miss the sidebar. So my earlier notes on the sidebar remain, right? The kind of sidebar I want can expand into the sources and have a 'Show more' option. The count and the logos of the companies are all that are needed. The name/handle switch can be removed, I think. I think the page is looking blank because it doesn't have a header. What do you think? This feed looks much better, but it's just devoid of any life, I'd say. Perhaps that's because I've been looking at the same six examples instead of seeing a live feed in action. Onboarding is much better for the one now. Since the left side is already showing the steps, finding X profile is fine for farzanmrz. The 'Reading your newest post' section can stream below, so the username comes on the right side. You don't need to show the pinned post, or you can, and each post can just come below there as the 'Reading your newest post' section is going on the page. Gathering candidates needs to have some animation there, and checking relevance needs to have some animation. Choosing sources: what happens then is that your brief comes right at the top of the right sidebar, and the center is free to show just the sources themselves. Does that make sense? The accounts, the sites, the feeds: are you understanding what I'm saying? I like how, in the Deck onboarding building design, you show strong match, possible match, and set-aside content like that. We can take the center of the page for that. Does that make sense? The right side is for the user's own stuff, and the left side is for my timeline. Is that all right? Can we render this now? I'm unhappy with the login. I'm still not liking it. I like the login for the Deck more than the current one, and I don't know why. I think your way of separating the login from the cards is not nice. Can you please look at some React Bits Pro component for the login and put it there? Notifications are fine, but I guess now that we're introducing the sidebar or the header, it'll change a bit. There's a problem with the setup page: it's a fact that, without a user's X account, the agent is not proceeding, right? That doesn't mean they have to connect it, and the setup page simply needs to be a precursor to the onboarding page. On the onboarding page, the top should have 'X account' and 'Build my agent' at the right, and the heading should change as follows: Choosing sources; Saving your agent. We need a neat way of representing this. Does that make sense? As far as your sources page is concerned, when I click on Vercel, it shows the description for Vercel, but on other accounts, it doesn't. What does that mean? There should be no numbers next to the sources because this is the sources page. The account and handle can come next to each other, and the website and name can come next to each other. There needs to be the ability to add or remove sources, and I'm guessing there also needs to be a settings page, maybe because that's where subscription and all will also come, right? The free week counter in the deck design, the card, and this week's card, I like those. I think that's what's devoid of life in our current feed. Even X DM notifications, there won't be a toggle. There'll be a button because the plan is that this takes them to their X website, where they have to DM the bot. A lot of these are open stuff that I've given, so do the needful, and then you can trigger a live feed for me and for Reshad, so at least I can see the actual examples. The page itself is looking devoid of life, I guess. Maybe the top of the page has those pill-style filters that view by only RSS feeds, view by only this source, etc., in clustered and direct both. I don't know. The banner itself looks good, but maybe it can be some other UI than the cards. The card UI itself, I don't like. For notifications, it's irrelevant, but even for sources, that's a bit weird because a person should be able to add and remove sources as per their limit count. It's just a bunch of things that I'm confused about which direction to go in, but it's moving in a positive direction. Discuss with council and then do the needful accordingly.\"\n\n## What to read (under /Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/)\n- Renders now (focus-review/renders/): feed-open.png, feed-menu.png, feed-wide.png (pass 10); onboarding-step-1.png, onboarding-mid.png, onboarding-done.png; login.png; setup.png; sources.png; notifications.png. Deck pieces he names: deck-feed.png (its three tiles: Checking, This week, Free week; its source sidebar with logos, counts, 3 per group then Show more), deck-login.png, deck-building.png (strong match, possible match, set aside).\n- Code: site/v2/one/{rail,feed,card,onboarding,login,setup,sources,notifications}.tsx; Deck: site/v2/deck/{feed,chrome,stack,marks,live,data,building}.tsx and site/next/building/steps.ts (the 8 engine steps).\n- His history: focus-review/history/owner-history.md (every design message, verbatim; loves, hates, reversals at the end). His sidebar words there: Oct 3 \"pick it exactly as it appears in the deck... 3 items before Show more... numbers aligned\"; Oct 3 \"no reduced sidebar... When it's closed, it's closed\"; Oct 4 07:46 \"the sidebar thingy can float atop the page\" (like the Next.js dev bubble); Oct 4 pass 8 \"the collab sidebar should be a button by itself, first thing\"; then the bubble menu (pass 9). His tiles words: Oct 4 pass 8 \"Get rid of the three cards up top\"; today \"The free week counter in the deck design, the card, and this week's card, I like those... that's what's devoid of life\".\n- React Bits Pro: the lab has the paid registry wired (site/components.json, @reactbits-pro) and the skill at /Users/farzanm4/.agents/skills/react-bits-pro/SKILL.md lists auth blocks auth-1..6 and authentication-1..14. A file focus-review/reactbits-auth.md may exist by the time you read, describing each auth block's layout; if it does not, judge from the skill.\n- Facts: the Sources page shows a reason under a clicked source only when the sample data has a \"focus\" text for it (sources.tsx line 75, deck/data.ts); in the product every chosen source has its reason. The onboarding replay is a fixed script (next/building/steps.ts); a live feed needs the product app with a real agent built for him and for Reshad.\n\n## Questions (answer each with one consensus-shaped position; name where you expect the others to differ)\n1. Feed chrome. He misses the sidebar (Deck's source list: logos and counts, 3 per group then Show more, no name/handle switch, expands and collapses fully, floating over the page per his Oct 4 words) and thinks the page lacks a header. The bubble menu exists. Give ONE composition: what the sidebar holds, how it opens (floating over the page, from the bubble or its own button), whether a header exists and what is in it (Feed title, Clustered/Direct, the free-week counter, the \"this week\" card), where the tiles he now misses go without recreating the \"three cards up top\" he removed, whether pill filters by kind or source belong at the top (he said \"I don't know\"), and what the DM banner becomes if not a card.\n2. Onboarding. Turn his paragraph into a column spec: left = the 8-step timeline; right = his own things (profile at the top, then the posts streaming in under \"Reading your newest posts\", then the brief at the top of the right column from \"Choose sources\" on); center = Gather candidates and Check relevance with motion (say what moves), then the candidates as strong match, possible match, set aside (Deck building), then the chosen sources by kind. Top right: \"X account\" and \"Build my agent\" controls; the heading changes from \"Choosing sources\" to \"Saving your agent\" to \"Your agent is ready\". Say what the setup page keeps as the precursor (handle and sentence only?) and what moves to onboarding.\n3. Login. He likes Deck's login more and dislikes the form separated from the cards. Choose: Deck's login as is, or a React Bits Pro auth block (name the slug and why it fits DESIGN.md's fixed theme), with the story cards how.\n4. Sources page. No counts; account and handle on one row, site and name on one row; add and remove sources against a limit (how the limit shows); he dislikes the card UI here. Give the list anatomy. Say whether a Settings page (subscription, account) should be built now as the One or wait.\n5. Notifications. The X DM row becomes a button that opens X to DM the bot (no toggle). Anything else.\n6. Live feed. He wants to see the feed update live, for himself and for Reshad. Options: the lab's replay made longer and visibly live (new stories arriving); or the product app run locally on another port with his real account and a real build; or oparax.ai after the next conversion. Pick one for this week and say the cost in his time.\n7. Order. One Opus builder, one pass, then he walks localhost: which pages first, and the 2 questions to ask him after.\n\nDeliver: RESULT: FINDINGS, then sections 1 to 7, each a numbered spec of concrete items tied to his words (quote him), at most 8 lines per section. No em dashes. Plain words; he reads this.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":25,"fileSize":9722,"path":"/Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-next-oct4/brief.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":25},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"Read_0_cba3cf76-f7091","startedAtMs":"1791160984731","completedAtMs":"1791160985014"},"model_call_id":"d5600c43-863d-4bb6-95b5-b3820da80b32-0-na7e","session_id":"881c6847-9f61-41b3-b161-f9f1b5554e95","timestamp_ms":1791160985041}
